content:
maria: Quick heads-up — want a very short design sync on playground streaming controls. Thinking: replace the big 'Stop' button with a softer 'Interrupt' behavior, make compact token hint sticky, and add a quick-insert flow in the prompt library. Figma: https://figma.com/file/REDACTED. Thoughts?
kevin: I like the 'Interrupt' language — less scary for users. Suggest change icon to a pause+slash instead of a red square. Also propose microcopy for compact token hint: '~120 tokens used' vs '120 tokens (est)'.
leah: Accessibility nits: whichever label we pick needs an aria-label that describes the effect, e.g., `Interrupt generation — preserves partial response`. Also keyboard support: both Enter and Space should trigger, and focus order must not skip the token pill.
ash: Engineering constraints: two behaviors here — soft interrupt (lets model finish current token/batched op) vs hard abort (drop request). Soft is doable but we need to keep KV cache intact and mark the session partial. That implies change to streaming protocol: add `interrupt` flag in the request envelope. Pseudocode:```js
// server-side handling
if (action === 'interrupt') {
  stream.signal('interrupt');
  keepKvCache = true;
} else {
  stream.abort();
  clearKvCache();
}
```
sam: From telemetry/devex POV: track `ui.stop_click` with `mode: soft|hard`, and emit `token_estimate` when the compact hint shows. For prompt library quick-insert, propose hotkey `Ctrl+Shift+P` and an event `prompt_quick_insert`.
kevin: UI detail: compact state shouldn't show live token counter (which jitters). Show an estimate with lower opacity and tooltip that opens on hover: `Estimated tokens for current input`. For streaming, show an aria-live region for interim text so screen readers read partial output.
leah: +1 to aria-live. Also ensure the interrupt button has `aria-pressed` state during streaming so AT knows generation is active. Tooltip copy should be available to assistive tech.
maria: Microcopy options for the button (need to pick one):
1) Interrupt — preserves partial output
2) Pause generation — you can resume
3) Stop generation — abort immediately
Which do folks prefer?
ash: From infra side, option 2 (Pause) implies resume semantics — that's heavier because we need to rehydrate model state to continue. Option 1 (Interrupt) is simplest: it stops streaming but keeps prompt + KV so user can regenerate.
kevin: I vote for 1) Interrupt. UI note: show secondary action on hover 'Regenerate' and keep affordance for quick retry.
sam: For prompt library UX: quick-insert preview should show token delta before insertion, like `+34 tokens`. Use muted text and small icon. Hotkey + CTA on card — agree with `Ctrl+Shift+P`.
leah: A11y checklist before ship: keyboard nav to prompt cards, visible focus ring, clear contrast on token badge (WCAG AA), aria-live for streaming area, and ensure change announcements are concise.
maria: OK — plan: go with 'Interrupt' microcopy, implement soft interrupt with `keepKvCache`, compact token hint shows `~<n> tokens` with tooltip, hotkey for prompt quick-insert `Ctrl+Shift+P`. Kevin -> update Figma and hand off assets. Ash -> draft API `interrupt` flag and telemetry events. Leah -> run quick a11y pass on new states. Sam -> add telemetry events to tracking doc. I'll update the ticket and add owners. :thumbsup:
devops-bot: Deploy preview job queued for branch `playground/stop-interrupt-ux` — builds start in ~5m. 
kevin: Noted — I'll push the figma update in a bit.
maria: Thanks everyone — small follow-ups in the ticket.
